This repository and the npm package also carry third-party files under their own licences:

- Inter, EB Garamond and JetBrains Mono typefaces (woff2 files from fontsource), under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1. Each copy sits beside its licence: packages/player/fonts/OFL-*.txt in the package, and
  assets/fonts/OFL-*.txt in each video's folder (videos/ and .reelplanner/).

- GSAP (https://gsap.com), under the GSAP Standard License (https://gsap.com/standard-license). Copies of
  gsap.min.js, with its licence header, are in the example videos (videos/*/assets/vendor/); reelplanner
  installs it as an npm dependency and copies it into a video's folder when it builds one.

- HyperFrames (https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), under the Apache License 2.0, is an npm
  dependency; the review page reelplanner builds bundles its player and runtime.

- The sketch page (`reelplanner sketch`) runs on Excalidraw (https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw, MIT) and
  React (MIT), optional npm dependencies that `vendor-excalidraw` bundles once per machine into
  ~/.reelplanner/vendor/, the bundle opening with Excalidraw's licence and keeping React's; nothing of them is in this
  repository or the package.
  Excalidraw's npm package carries its fonts, copied beside that bundle: Excalifont, Virgil, Xiaolai, Nunito, Lilita
  One, Assistant and Cascadia under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, Comic Shanns under MIT, and Liberation Sans 1.05
  under the GPL 2 with its font exception (fonts/LICENSES.md there). A sketch's pictures and recording are drawn with
  them; no font file goes into a sketch.
